WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.816 --> 00:00:05.318
&gt;&gt; Cosmos is yours.

00:00:05.451 --> 00:00:08.755
Come with me.

00:00:08.888 --> 00:00:14.694
&gt;&gt; Neal Degrass Tyson, I was

00:00:14.828 --> 00:00:17.363
going to wear that exact tie.

00:00:17.497 --> 00:00:18.331
&gt;&gt; No you were not.

00:00:18.464 --> 00:00:18.965
You are lying.

00:00:19.098 --> 00:00:22.268
&gt;&gt; I promise you, I do not have

00:00:22.502 --> 00:00:24.237
a tie like that in my closet.

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:25.605
&gt;&gt; I have 110 ties.

00:00:25.738 --> 00:00:28.942
Each one is uniquely capturing

00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:31.277
in the up verse as imagined as

00:00:31.411 --> 00:00:33.279
felt through the eyes of an

00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:33.613
artist.

00:00:33.746 --> 00:00:35.181
&gt;&gt; I want to start with your

00:00:35.315 --> 00:00:39.619
latest book "Story messenger."

00:00:39.752 --> 00:00:41.855
In your book, you use the device

00:00:42.255 --> 00:00:44.457
of saying what would an alien

00:00:44.591 --> 00:00:44.724
say?

00:00:44.858 --> 00:00:46.492
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:00:46.626 --> 00:00:47.193
&gt;&gt; If they came here to Earth

00:00:47.327 --> 00:00:47.694
from outer space.

00:00:47.827 --> 00:00:48.261
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:00:48.261 --> 00:00:50.663
&gt;&gt; And they saw our wars, our

00:00:50.797 --> 00:00:52.432
politics, as you say, our

00:00:52.565 --> 00:00:53.900
inability to distinguish fact

00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:55.668
from opinion.

00:00:55.802 --> 00:00:58.271
So what do you think said alien

00:00:58.271 --> 00:00:58.671
would say?

00:00:58.805 --> 00:01:03.009
&gt;&gt; So the alien comes upon

00:01:03.142 --> 00:01:07.213
Earth, beautiful blue marble

00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:08.748
orbiting the sun and there is

00:01:08.882 --> 00:01:10.283
ocean and land and clouds and

00:01:10.283 --> 00:01:12.285
learn there is a species that

00:01:12.285 --> 00:01:13.519
spread itself across all the

00:01:13.653 --> 00:01:13.820
land.

00:01:13.953 --> 00:01:17.523
Oh, that's a very productive

00:01:17.657 --> 00:01:18.758
productive,

00:01:18.892 --> 00:01:19.492
successful species and come down

00:01:19.626 --> 00:01:21.761
and say wait a minute, that same

00:01:21.895 --> 00:01:25.498
species has drawn lines on this

00:01:25.632 --> 00:01:26.499
otherwise continuous set of land

00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:28.301
masses and these lines you can't

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:29.335
cross them unless you have

00:01:29.469 --> 00:01:31.137
special papers, not only that,

00:01:31.271 --> 00:01:33.473
they have divided themselves by

00:01:33.606 --> 00:01:36.342
who they worship, who their skin

00:01:36.476 --> 00:01:39.479
color is, what their -- how they

00:01:39.612 --> 00:01:41.281
dress, where resources are and

00:01:41.414 --> 00:01:42.315
where they're not.

00:01:42.315 --> 00:01:46.452
On a level where they will even

00:01:46.586 --> 00:01:51.424
commit violence, even all out

00:01:51.557 --> 00:01:51.724
war.

00:01:51.858 --> 00:01:53.026
&gt;&gt; But we do have real

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:54.327
differences, serious differences

00:01:54.327 --> 00:01:55.595
between nations, between

00:01:55.728 --> 00:01:57.530
political parties.

00:01:57.664 --> 00:01:59.165
Are we just supposed to say from

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:01.234
a cosmic perspective they don't

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:01.567
matter?

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:03.603
&gt;&gt; No, no.

00:02:03.736 --> 00:02:07.106
In fact, the differences enrich

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.509
the plurality of a nation,

00:02:09.642 --> 00:02:10.343
especially a free nation.

00:02:10.443 --> 00:02:12.345
I don't want to get rid of

00:02:12.345 --> 00:02:12.512
differences.

00:02:12.645 --> 00:02:18.918
I want to get rid of differences

00:02:19.052 --> 00:02:20.019
that are not different.

00:02:20.353 --> 00:02:21.354
You think different because you

00:02:21.487 --> 00:02:22.622
dug your heels into some opinion

00:02:22.755 --> 00:02:24.424
that is malformed based on what

00:02:24.557 --> 00:02:26.826
you think is true.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.695
That's different from us

00:02:28.828 --> 00:02:31.998
agreeingbjectively

00:02:32.365 --> 00:02:33.466
true and sitting down saying

00:02:33.599 --> 00:02:34.834
what do you think of this?

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:36.369
You share your point of view as

00:02:36.369 --> 00:02:36.803
do I.

00:02:36.936 --> 00:02:40.640
That's interesting.

00:02:40.773 --> 00:02:42.375
I haven't thought about it that

00:02:42.375 --> 00:02:42.508
way.

00:02:42.642 --> 00:02:43.810
Is there a way to resolve this?

00:02:43.943 --> 00:02:45.678
&gt;&gt; You have carved out a unique

00:02:45.812 --> 00:02:47.580
place for yourself in our

00:02:47.714 --> 00:02:49.682
intellectual life these days.

00:02:49.816 --> 00:02:51.050
And I think, I don't know if

00:02:51.184 --> 00:02:53.019
you'll object to this, I would

00:02:53.152 --> 00:02:54.420
describe it as the pop

00:02:54.554 --> 00:02:55.388
scientist.

00:02:55.521 --> 00:02:57.857
Here you are on one of your many

00:02:57.991 --> 00:03:00.026
shows, cosmos possible world.

00:03:00.393 --> 00:03:03.096
Take a look.

00:03:03.229 --> 00:03:04.630
&gt;&gt; Every month represents about

00:03:05.665 --> 00:03:08.434
a billion years.

00:03:08.568 --> 00:03:10.470
Every day represents nearly 40

00:03:10.603 --> 00:03:11.104
million years.

00:03:11.237 --> 00:03:13.606
That first day of the cosmic

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:19.112
year began with the big bang.

00:03:19.245 --> 00:03:24.417
Almost 14 billion years ago.

00:03:24.517 --> 00:03:26.019
Nothing really happened in our

00:03:26.419 --> 00:03:28.087
neck of the universe until about

00:03:28.421 --> 00:03:30.757
3 billion years later.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:33.326
March 15th of the cosmic year.

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:37.030
When our milky way galaxy began

00:03:37.163 --> 00:03:37.930
to form.

00:03:38.064 --> 00:03:42.435
&gt;&gt; How did you decide on this

00:03:42.435 --> 00:03:45.905
role and do you get push back

00:03:46.039 --> 00:03:49.542
and I say this advisedly serious

00:03:49.675 --> 00:03:49.942
scientist.

00:03:50.076 --> 00:03:52.011
&gt;&gt; That pop scientist role had

00:03:52.445 --> 00:03:53.946
already been carved by Carl

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.749
Sagan and whatever blood on the

00:03:56.883 --> 00:03:58.651
tracks that left, I remember

00:03:58.785 --> 00:04:00.920
hearing about this that he was

00:04:01.054 --> 00:04:03.089
chastised by colleagues for

00:04:03.222 --> 00:04:08.795
appearing on "Tonight show" with

00:04:08.928 --> 00:04:10.563
Johnny Carson and had reach into

00:04:10.696 --> 00:04:13.766
the tax paying public so at some

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.635
level we have a duty, if not an

00:04:15.768 --> 00:04:16.803
obligation to bring some of that

00:04:16.936 --> 00:04:18.104
back to the public and yeah,

00:04:18.471 --> 00:04:19.772
when I'm writing a back, I'm not

00:04:19.906 --> 00:04:21.741
doing the research paper.

00:04:21.874 --> 00:04:22.041
Right?

00:04:22.475 --> 00:04:24.110
So there is a tradeoff often in

00:04:24.477 --> 00:04:24.544
that.

00:04:24.544 --> 00:04:26.746
But no, I still have strong

00:04:26.879 --> 00:04:29.248
roots into the research

00:04:29.382 --> 00:04:29.649
community.

00:04:29.782 --> 00:04:31.150
&gt;&gt; You were involved in the

00:04:31.284 --> 00:04:34.954
effort to demote Pluto.

00:04:35.088 --> 00:04:38.491
You even appeared on my favorite

00:04:38.491 --> 00:04:40.493
science show "Big bang theory".

00:04:40.526 --> 00:04:40.726
&gt;&gt; Oh.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:42.495
&gt;&gt; Here it is.

00:04:42.528 --> 00:04:43.029
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.162 --> 00:04:45.898
&gt;&gt; I'm quite familiar with Dr.

00:04:46.032 --> 00:04:46.499
Tyson.

00:04:46.499 --> 00:04:49.268
He's responsible for the

00:04:49.402 --> 00:04:50.503
demotion of Pluto.

00:04:50.636 --> 00:04:54.674
I liked Pluto.

00:04:54.807 --> 00:04:56.709
Ergo, I do not like you.

00:04:56.843 --> 00:05:01.981
&gt;&gt; I didn't demote Pluto.

00:05:02.115 --> 00:05:03.316
That was a vote of the union.

00:05:03.449 --> 00:05:07.854
&gt;&gt; If IFS and buts were nuts,

00:05:07.987 --> 00:05:09.956
we'd all have a merry Christmas.

00:05:10.089 --> 00:05:10.690
&gt;&gt; I can't act.

00:05:10.823 --> 00:05:12.024
&gt;&gt; I thought you did well.

00:05:12.158 --> 00:05:13.159
&gt;&gt; Did I do okay?

00:05:13.292 --> 00:05:13.526
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:05:13.659 --> 00:05:17.029
&gt;&gt; Is it true you got hate mail

00:05:17.163 --> 00:05:18.731
for dissing Pluto?

00:05:18.865 --> 00:05:19.298
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:05:19.432 --> 00:05:21.167
I got a file cabinet this deep

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:22.068
from third graders.

00:05:22.201 --> 00:05:24.871
&gt;&gt; Third grade, I learned how

00:05:25.004 --> 00:05:25.571
you can tell the planets from

00:05:25.705 --> 00:05:31.010
their distance from the sun,

00:05:31.144 --> 00:05:32.645
Mary's violet eyes make John

00:05:32.778 --> 00:05:34.714
stay up nights period.

00:05:34.847 --> 00:05:36.549
Period.

00:05:36.549 --> 00:05:36.616
Pluto.

00:05:36.749 --> 00:05:37.817
Now there's no period.

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.418
&gt;&gt; So deal with it.

00:05:39.552 --> 00:05:39.819
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.952 --> 00:05:41.487
I'm just saying.

00:05:41.621 --> 00:05:42.722
&gt;&gt; All right.

00:05:42.855 --> 00:05:46.559
In a minute, why is Pluto not a

00:05:46.559 --> 00:05:47.093
planet?

00:05:47.226 --> 00:05:54.600
&gt;&gt; Pluto's orbit is

00:05:54.734 --> 00:05:55.334
significantly tipped out of the

00:05:55.468 --> 00:05:56.802
plane of orbits of other

00:05:56.936 --> 00:05:57.136
planets.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:59.071
More than half of Pluto's volume

00:05:59.205 --> 00:06:00.573
is comprised of ice.

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:01.841
If you brought Pluto to where

00:06:01.974 --> 00:06:03.543
Earth is now, heat from the sun

00:06:03.676 --> 00:06:05.611
would evaporate that ice and

00:06:05.745 --> 00:06:06.612
grow a tail.

00:06:06.746 --> 00:06:08.848
That's not behavior for a

00:06:08.981 --> 00:06:09.182
planet.

00:06:09.315 --> 00:06:11.117
&gt;&gt; Do you believe that there is

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.652
life out there somewhere?

00:06:12.785 --> 00:06:14.587
&gt;&gt; I would say that if there

00:06:14.587 --> 00:06:16.622
weren't life, it would be

00:06:16.756 --> 00:06:17.023
astonishing.

00:06:17.156 --> 00:06:21.460
If -- given how common our

00:06:21.594 --> 00:06:23.162
ingredients are and how quickly

00:06:23.296 --> 00:06:27.066
life took place and how many

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.235
planets are orbiting the stars.

00:06:29.368 --> 00:06:31.304
&gt;&gt; What about aliens and ufos.

00:06:31.437 --> 00:06:32.972
&gt;&gt; Any life is aliens.

00:06:33.105 --> 00:06:37.076
You mean are antennas and ray

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:37.376
guns?

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:39.412
&gt;&gt; Anything without a cell.

00:06:39.545 --> 00:06:40.947
&gt;&gt; Something that could land in

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:41.347
a spaceship?

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:42.615
Could be out there.

00:06:42.615 --> 00:06:44.116
There is no evidence that would

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.954
convince an authentic skeptic

00:06:48.087 --> 00:06:48.754
that we've been visited and I

00:06:48.888 --> 00:06:55.027
can tell you this, these fuzzy

00:06:55.161 --> 00:06:57.463
monocramtic tick tacks that show

00:06:57.597 --> 00:06:59.565
up on Navy restricted air space

00:06:59.699 --> 00:07:01.934
in our own atmosphere, by the

00:07:02.068 --> 00:07:03.369
way, you've seen the high

00:07:03.502 --> 00:07:04.837
resolution images from a

00:07:04.971 --> 00:07:06.272
telescope we parked a million

00:07:06.639 --> 00:07:09.208
miles from Earth called the

00:07:09.342 --> 00:07:10.676
James Webb space telescope

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:11.477
looking at the edge of the

00:07:11.611 --> 00:07:12.645
universe and the best you have

00:07:12.778 --> 00:07:15.715
of visiting aliens is a fuzzy

00:07:15.848 --> 00:07:16.716
tick tack?

00:07:16.849 --> 00:07:19.085
You got to do better than that

00:07:19.218 --> 00:07:26.125
if you convince an astro

00:07:26.259 --> 00:07:26.659
physist.

00:07:26.659 --> 00:07:35.101
&gt;&gt; You go to the planetarium,

00:07:35.234 --> 00:07:37.103
changed your mind, why?

00:07:37.236 --> 00:07:37.837
&gt;&gt; Sometimes I wonder if I grew

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.238
up on a farm somewhere I

00:07:39.372 --> 00:07:40.840
wouldn't be as star struck as I

00:07:40.973 --> 00:07:43.209
was because there I am a kid

00:07:43.342 --> 00:07:44.744
having grown up until the bronx.

00:07:44.877 --> 00:07:45.444
&gt;&gt; Right.

00:07:45.578 --> 00:07:46.912
&gt;&gt; You sit in a chair.

00:07:47.046 --> 00:07:47.713
The lights dim.

00:07:47.847 --> 00:07:49.415
The stars come out and more

00:07:49.548 --> 00:07:50.883
stars than I ever seen in my

00:07:51.017 --> 00:07:51.183
life.

00:07:51.317 --> 00:07:52.685
A hoax for sure.

00:07:52.752 --> 00:07:55.755
I know how many stars are in the

00:07:55.888 --> 00:07:56.222
night sky.

00:07:56.355 --> 00:07:56.922
There is six visible from the

00:07:57.056 --> 00:07:57.256
bronx.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.691
That was the night sky.

00:07:58.691 --> 00:07:59.925
No one in New York City has any

00:08:00.059 --> 00:08:01.527
kind of relationship with the

00:08:01.661 --> 00:08:01.927
night sky.

00:08:02.061 --> 00:08:02.695
&gt;&gt; It's true.

00:08:02.695 --> 00:08:05.197
When you go out into the real

00:08:05.331 --> 00:08:06.332
world, it's like what are all

00:08:06.699 --> 00:08:07.066
those lights?

00:08:07.199 --> 00:08:08.701
&gt;&gt; What are all those lights?

00:08:08.834 --> 00:08:11.404
There they dim the lights and

00:08:11.537 --> 00:08:13.205
I'm struck by it.

00:08:13.339 --> 00:08:14.240
Whereas had I seen that every

00:08:14.373 --> 00:08:16.075
night of my life, this would be,

00:08:16.208 --> 00:08:17.710
of course, this was just the

00:08:17.843 --> 00:08:18.210
night sky.

00:08:18.344 --> 00:08:19.478
So this -- it hit me.

00:08:19.612 --> 00:08:21.280
So I don't think I chose the

00:08:21.414 --> 00:08:22.381
universe, I think the universe

00:08:22.715 --> 00:08:26.719
chose

00:08:26.752 --> 00:08:28.721
&gt;&gt; You talk about your journey.

00:08:28.721 --> 00:08:30.723
You used this phrase as the path

00:08:30.723 --> 00:08:32.391
of most resistance.

00:08:32.725 --> 00:08:34.927
A young black kid from the bronx

00:08:35.061 --> 00:08:38.731
becoming an astrophysicist.

00:08:38.731 --> 00:08:40.399
How tough was that path?

00:08:40.733 --> 00:08:41.467
How important do you think it

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:45.538
has been for people of color to

00:08:45.671 --> 00:08:46.372
see you in the place that you

00:08:46.739 --> 00:08:49.041
occupy?

00:08:49.175 --> 00:08:51.711
&gt;&gt; I will invert that and say,

00:08:51.844 --> 00:08:53.546
how important is it for white

00:08:53.679 --> 00:08:57.183
people to see me where I am?

00:08:57.316 --> 00:08:59.819
That's a way more important

00:08:59.952 --> 00:09:03.189
force operating, especially if

00:09:03.322 --> 00:09:04.990
that is the community that

00:09:05.124 --> 00:09:06.759
wields resources and

00:09:06.892 --> 00:09:07.193
opportunities.

00:09:07.326 --> 00:09:08.761
And if you see a black homeless

00:09:08.761 --> 00:09:10.062
person in the street and you

00:09:10.196 --> 00:09:12.998
never saw a black academically

00:09:13.132 --> 00:09:15.267
achieved other human being, you

00:09:15.401 --> 00:09:16.769
are prone to say, that's just

00:09:16.802 --> 00:09:18.237
their lot in life.

00:09:18.371 --> 00:09:21.307
But now, you will see me and you

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:22.975
will see the black homeless

00:09:23.109 --> 00:09:24.310
person, and you have to deal

00:09:24.443 --> 00:09:25.711
with that.

00:09:25.845 --> 00:09:28.347
Oh, my gosh, there but for the

00:09:28.781 --> 00:09:31.050
lack of opportunity goes --

00:09:31.183 --> 00:09:31.650
&gt;&gt; A lot of people?

00:09:31.784 --> 00:09:34.053
&gt;&gt; A lot of people.

00:09:34.186 --> 00:09:37.022
I want to put that up front.

00:09:37.156 --> 00:09:38.958
It was the path of most

00:09:39.091 --> 00:09:40.259
resistance because I was also

00:09:40.393 --> 00:09:41.994
physically fit and athletic.

00:09:42.128 --> 00:09:43.629
You see a black person who is

00:09:43.763 --> 00:09:45.498
that, particularly in the day,

00:09:45.631 --> 00:09:46.932
you should be an athlete.

00:09:47.066 --> 00:09:51.404
That just simply fulfills

00:09:51.537 --> 00:09:54.807
people's bin they would put you

00:09:54.807 --> 00:09:55.574
because they have never seen

00:09:55.708 --> 00:09:57.510
your kind do anything else.

00:09:57.643 --> 00:09:59.412
My father, who is active with

00:09:59.545 --> 00:10:03.048
the civil rights movement, he

00:10:03.182 --> 00:10:05.751
had way worse life encounters

00:10:05.885 --> 00:10:08.821
than I did, dealing with

00:10:08.821 --> 00:10:08.854
society.

00:10:08.988 --> 00:10:10.823
He was never bitter.

00:10:10.823 --> 00:10:13.726
He said, these people don't know

00:10:13.859 --> 00:10:14.059
better.

00:10:14.193 --> 00:10:15.928
So I have carried that with me

00:10:16.061 --> 00:10:16.829
ever since.

00:10:16.829 --> 00:10:17.963
I have never been bitter.

00:10:18.097 --> 00:10:19.965
It just is.

